<%# The "You May Also Like" section. The build renders it from the order that the api calculates
    from the article text and the concepts (data/related.json, through `rake import:related`). It
    renders nothing when the entry has no neighbor, and that is what removed the widget that this
    section replaced.

    ⚠️ scope_entry_ids is necessary: read_next renders more summary cards on this same page, and an
    entry with a near meaning is often also the adjacent entry in time. Without the section in the
    id, the two cards would have the same DOM id and both aria-labelledby values would point at the
    first card. `article` is a necessary local. %>
<% related = related_articles(article) %>
<% if related.present? %>
  <%= partial 'partials/collection', locals: { title: "You May Also Like", items: related, variant: "halves", scope_entry_ids: true } %>
<% end %>
